WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:01.620
(applause)

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.540
- Welcome back to TCSN.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.580
We have a really special offer for you.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.200
It's a turkey cheddar sandwich.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.880
- Wow, look at that.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.060
- This is handmade with
avocado, tomato and lettuce

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.190
on an artisanal whole wheat baguette

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.600
and it can be yours for only

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.783
four easy installments of 2.99.

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:19.650
- That is a great deal.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:20.820
Now I don't know about you,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.330
but I like my sandwiches
with chips and a drink.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.320
- We've got you covered.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.153
Look at this.

00:00:26.153 --> 00:00:28.200
A bag of salt and vinegar potato chips

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.450
for three payments of 89 cents

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:34.440
and a diet Dr. Dinky cola for
only six payments of 49 cents.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.723
- Whoa, I'm sold and hungry.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.700
How do I sign up?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.710
- Just send us your name, phone number,

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.720
date of birth and social security number

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.430
and you can get approved in seconds.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.633
- So easy.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.380
- Paying for a sandwich in installments

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.390
may seem absurd to some,

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.880
but the practice is becoming
more and more popular

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.460
especially among younger shoppers.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.050
- Buy now, pay later loans

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.550
are one of the hottest new trends

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.590
in the world of financial technology,

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.770
touted as a less risky
alternative to credit cards.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.780
Using one of several major apps

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.400
you're only asked for a fraction

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.080
of the price at the point of sale

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.370
and the rest is paid off

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.200
in a few biweekly installments.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.610
As long as you pay on time,

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:15.780
there's no interest.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.012
- No interest?

00:01:17.012 --> 00:01:18.561
- Oh, hold on Turbo,

00:01:18.561 --> 00:01:20.640
it might sound like a no-brainer,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.350
but any savvy spender knows

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.870
you don't dive headfirst
into a new financial tool

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.670
without digging a little deeper.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.160
How do BNPL loans really work?

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.761
What are the drawbacks and dangers

00:01:30.761 --> 00:01:33.823
and what's in it for the
companies that offer them?

00:01:33.823 --> 00:01:36.406
(upbeat music)

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.850
- Times were tough during
the Great Depression

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.340
and people weren't
spending like they used to.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.320
So merchants came up with a new system

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.700
called a layaway plan

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.790
which allowed shoppers to put
a deposit down on a purchase

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.040
and pay the rest off in installments.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.720
When the balance is fully paid off,

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.203
the merchandise is delivered.

00:01:59.203 --> 00:02:02.313
- Layaway plans were
popular up until the 1980s

00:02:02.313 --> 00:02:04.260
when credit cards replaced them

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.060
as the preferred way to buy things

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.500
with money you don't have.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.180
But over the last four decades

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.910
many Americans have
soured on credit cards,

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.160
associating them with
high interest payments

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.350
and lifelong debt spirals.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.420
- So it's no wonder that young people

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.360
are starting to embrace
Buy Now Pay Later loans

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.960
as a kind of modern tech
reboot of the layaway plan.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.160
Like layaway plans,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.800
they have a no interest
installment structure,

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.910
but like credit cards,

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.890
you receive the purchase immediately.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.380
You don't have to wait until
the balance is paid off.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.270
- If you think this
sounds like a good deal,

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:37.500
you're not alone.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.540
Between 2019 and 2021,

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.870
the total value of BNPL
loans from the major lenders

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.180
grew more than a thousand percent

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.930
from around 2 billion to over 24 billion.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.390
The value of transactions
financed this way

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:55.620
quadrupled globally,
hitting over 120 billion.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.310
More than 40% of Americans
have used BNPL loans

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:02.250
and they're especially
popular with younger people,

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.190
who make up about half the user base.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.660
- And they seem to like it.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.250
According to consumer reports,

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.070
most users report being
satisfied with the service

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.640
and a survey by associate
marketing Professor Anastasia Ghosh

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.350
found that unlike credit cards,

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.330
consumers felt virtually no guilt

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.730
about using BNPL loans.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.940
- This is the part where
we say, however, isn't it?

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.960
- Yes, it is.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.750
However, there are drawbacks to BNPL loans

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.100
that consumer rights advocates

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.960
are trying to sound the alarm on.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.780
These are extremely new
financial inventions,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.629
which means they're largely unregulated.

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:37.290
The Truth in Lending Act,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.940
which protects you from unfair

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.040
or inaccurate credit practices,

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.410
doesn't apply to Buy Now, Pay Later.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.240
They don't have the rewards programs

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.830
or protections of credit cards,

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.200
which means you might not
be able to get a refund

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.230
if your purchase is lost
or damaged in transit.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.970
- And just because there's no interest

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.850
doesn't mean there aren't
penalties for late payments.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.330
Delinquency rates for BNPL
loans have been steadily growing

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.950
over the last few years,

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.220
as have loans charged off as bad debt.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.120
When this happens,

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.160
your credit rating takes a hit,

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.290
but the reverse is not true.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.680
Most BNPL companies don't
report on-time payments

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:14.820
to the credit bureaus,

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.800
which means they're not a viable way

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.690
to build your credit history.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.780
- Also, one of BNPL'S
most attractive features,

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:22.830
its ease of use,

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.510
is also a hazard.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:27.210
People are increasingly using
them for everyday purchases

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.960
like groceries, utility
bills, and yes sandwiches.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.460
This can lead to loan stacking

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.234
where borrowers quickly lose
track of multiple loans.

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:38.670
People who use BNPL loans
have seen a dramatic uptick

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.010
in overdraft fees and
because many have their

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.440
BNPL accounts tied to their credit cards,

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.600
they end up paying interest anyway.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.350
- But to understand the
true danger of BNPL loans,

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.720
we need to look at the business strategy

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.790
of the companies that offer them.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.030
These apps market themselves
as friendly, cool,

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.400
almost altruistic organizations

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.820
just trying to help you
live your best life, bro,

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.610
but we savvy shoppers
know that no corporation

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.000
does anything unless there's
something in it for them.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.440
Which begs the question,

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.490
how does a lender that doesn't
charge interest make money?

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.220
- The answer is merchant fees.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:20.220
Retailers pay BNPL companies to finance

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.300
their customers loans

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.390
and the fees are three
to four times higher

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.370
than those from credit card companies.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:27.930
Which begs another question,

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.530
why are merchants willing to
pay such exorbitant prices?

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.530
Because BNPL companies
are really, really good

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.690
at getting customers to spend more money.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.310
- If you're surfing an
online clothing store

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.900
with a hundred bucks to spend,

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.320
you might see a cute top that
usually goes for 80 bucks,

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.340
but you can have it right now
for a deposit of just $20.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:50.430
Throw in a shawl, a hat, pair of boots

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:54.336
and your $100 has financed
a whole new outfit...

00:05:54.336 --> 00:05:58.530
with about $300 in
installments to pay off.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:01.860
- A recent economic study
found that using BNPL loans

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.130
increases one's spending
habit by $60 a week,

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:09.420
bloating the average American's
retail budget by about 30%.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.370
Meanwhile, they're tracking your purchases

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.560
and collecting your data to develop more

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.290
effective ways to get you to spend more.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.340
As the director of the

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:19.650
Consumer Financial
Protection Bureau put it,

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.720
these firms aren't just lenders,

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:25.680
they're also advertisers
and virtual mall operators.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:28.860
- We have a tendency to
become entranced by new tech

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.950
and think that apps with
upbeat names and hip marketing

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.298
are really changing the
game for the better,

00:06:34.298 --> 00:06:36.090
but as we've seen before,

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:39.390
some tech companies are not so
much disrupting the industry

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.640
as just muscling their way into it.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.410
- That's why some
economists think that this

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.096
Buy Now, Pay Later fad
is just another loop

00:06:46.096 --> 00:06:49.020
in America's eternal credit cycle.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:50.820
It may seem like the shiny new thing,

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.521
but it will quickly lose its luster

00:06:52.521 --> 00:06:56.430
if consumers keep overspending
themselves into debt.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.770
- [Group] And that's our 2 cents.

